# Pull requests

## Title

Same as Conventional Commits: `type(optional-scope): subject`.

Type, scope, and subject are English.

## Body

Follow `.github/pull_request_template.md`. Same section headings, in this order:

1. `## Summary`
2. `## Related`
3. `## Test plan`
4. `## Verification`
5. `## Risk / Rollback`
6. `## Checklist`

- Headings and body text are English.
- Empty optional fields: write `N/A`. Do not delete the section.
- `Closes #N` is on its own line under `## Related` when the PR finishes that Issue. A PR that does not finish the issue names `#N` with no closing verb before the number (`.cursor/rules/github-closing.mdc`).
- An acceptance line the PR cannot fill (a number only another machine's tool gives, such as a Visual Studio sample share) means the PR does not finish the Issue. It names the missing line, says "Part of #N", and leaves the roadmap row `In progress` (#138, #139).
- When using `gh pr create`, pass a body that matches this template. Use a PowerShell here-string (`.cursor/rules/powershell-shell.mdc`).
- Do not invent alternate section names.
- Read the body again when its base merges and when a commit lands after it was written. A "Stacked on #N (base `branch`)" line is rewritten once #N merges and the base is `main`, and the Summary names every commit the head carries (#261, #265, #268).
- Edit a body from a file: write the current body to a UTF-8 file, change it, check that it is not empty, send it with `--body-file`, and read it back. A body sent through a pipe was emptied by a failed step in #263 and had a character damaged in #262.

Agents do not merge. A human squash-merges.
